    "### 4b. Binary classification - two-class `y`\n",
    "For subsets whose `y` is a genuine two-class label, correlation is not the natural summary.\n",
    "Use AUC: the probability that a randomly chosen positive item projects higher than a\n",
    "randomly chosen negative one. 0.5 = chance, 1.0 = perfect separation."
   ]
  },
